course: dictionary
lesson: 11529
title: Allotted: a share given out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Allotted means given out as a share for a purpose. When a teacher says «Each team has an allotted area», she means each team has a part of the space that was given to them. The clue is the word given: someone decided how much each team gets.
explain: Look at the words around it. «She had an allotted time of 30 minutes to finish the test.» The test has a set amount of time, and that set amount is the allotted time. Try swapping in the words given out or set aside. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: Allotted is also the past form of the verb allot. To allot means to give or share out a set amount. «The teacher allotted ten minutes to each group» means she gave out ten minutes to each group. Allot, allots, allotted and allotting are all forms of the same verb.
fact: Allotted means given out as a share for a purpose.
fact: «An allotted time» is the amount of time you are given to do something.
fact: Allot is the verb: to give or share out a set amount. Allotted is its past form.
fact: In a test, «finish within the allotted time» means do not go over the set time.
fact: In the UK, an allotment is a small piece of land rented for growing vegetables.
exercise: «Each team has an allotted area of the playground.» What does allotted mean here? | *Given out as a share for that team | Painted bright red | Shared with every other team at once | Lost and never found
exercise: Which word is the past form of allot? | allotting | allots | allotment | *allotted
exercise: «The teacher allotted ten minutes to each group.» What did the teacher do? | Ran a race against the clock | *Gave out a set amount of time to each group | Took away ten minutes | Forgot the time completely
test: «In the allotted 30 minutes, Sam answered 15 questions.» How many minutes did Sam have? | 45 | *30 | 2 | 15
test: Which phrase means do not go over the time? | Start early and stop late | Finish after the bell | *Finish within the allotted time | Take as long as you like
exam: Ben is allotted 8 stickers and gives 3 to his friend. How many stickers does he have left? | 8 | *5 | 3 | 11
